# === Self-hosted endpoint used by the attacker-behaviour-ladder experiments ===
# The adversarial/ladder runs use a self-hosted OpenAI-compatible (vLLM) endpoint,
# NOT the Anthropic default. Set BOTH of these, then run with
#   --model openai-chat:qwen35-122b --base-url "$OPENAI_BASE_URL"
# (and, because the endpoint is slow, --judge-timeout 120 --timeout 7200, or the
# ScopeJudge gate times out and fails closed). A ready-to-run recipe with all flags
# is experiments/run_ladder.sh.
# Ask the project owner for the key; it is a secret and must never be committed.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://inference.vulcan.alliancecan.ca/v1

# The Anthropic API key used by the default model (and by the post-hoc trajectory
# judge on scoped cases). Only needed for Claude-model runs, not the ladder.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Other sandbox-supported providers (`scopebench --list-models` shows slugs/keys).
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=...
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...

# Optional: override the model with any PydanticAI model string, e.g.
#   openai:gpt-5.2, google:gemini-2.5-pro, anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-5
# HARNESS_MODEL=anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-5

# Where `scopebench` finds the ScopeBench task dirs (no built-in
# default; alternatively pass --tasks-dir on each run).
# SCOPEBENCH_TASKS_DIR=/absolute/path/to/scopebench-tasks
